From 15d0fe58dd6fd58836e04cf32a77ad3c654401ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 16:21:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 236/254] fix(execution): close the report-only cross-block
 ground-truth gaps

The 0042 report-only probe found four report-internal ground-truth pairs that
were not cross-checked, plus fields assumed to have no report-local truth.

- report_binding_errors now enforces resolution.capability_digest vs
  capability.snapshot_digest, resolution.contract_digest vs
  resolved.contract.digest, dispatch.provider_declared vs fallback_chain[0] /
  resolved / invoked (fallback semantics preserved), and
  dispatch.fallback_used vs resolution.fallback_used
- guarantees.accumulation is re-derived from the registered OpDefinition
  contract and request.dtype; guarantees.exactness_basis from the invoked
  provider family; both are now must-reject instead of boundary entries
- artifact.pack.included_in_timing and resolution.plan_digest remain the
  documented single-document boundaries (external/manifest truth)
- tests: four cross-block must-reject cases plus two contract-derived
  guarantee cases and one genuine-report pass, runnable without AOCL
